{"id":"n-20261030-9tsjh6","category":"world","display_title":"AI Spending Rattles Wall Street","display_title_he":"ההוצאות על בינה מלאכותית מטלטלות את וול סטריט","short_summary":"Major tech giants including Google, Amazon, and Microsoft face investor scrutiny over astronomical spending on artificial intelligence, impacting stock values and profit margins.","english_level":"C1","words":421,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC News","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm9qzdqpxy48o","title":"Google value plunges by $500bn as AI fears rattle Wall Street","published_at":"2026-10-29T22:17:52.000Z"},{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/28/google-alphabet-q3-earnings-report","title":"Google owner Alphabet loses $500bn in market value after profit disappoints Wall Street","published_at":"2026-10-29T17:29:46.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-29T17:29:46.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-30T08:52:06.549Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The technology sector experienced a severe market reaction as astronomical financial commitments to artificial intelligence spooked investors across Wall Street. Google parent company Alphabet saw its total stock market value plunge by just over $500 billion, sending its stock to a six-month low. According to company updates, the sharp sell-off occurred after management revealed that AI-generated summaries on search engines were beginning to affect core advertising revenue, raising critical questions about balancing established businesses with expensive new technologies.","At first glance, Alphabet's quarterly financial results showed strong overall growth. Total revenue climbed 25% compared to the previous year, reaching $127.6 billion. This expansion was heavily buoyed by the remarkable success of Google Cloud, where revenue surged by 103% to nearly $31 billion, driven in part by in-house artificial intelligence chips known as TPUs. However, net profit slid by a considerable 25% down to $26.2 billion. Furthermore, Alphabet recorded a negative free cash flow exceeding $9 billion, indicating that the corporation is currently spending significantly more money on operations and capital investments than it generates.","According to industry analysts, these figures highlight the immense challenge of funding massive artificial intelligence infrastructure while maintaining the financial strength of traditional revenue streams. Alphabet's capital expenditures soared as the company poured funds into datacenters and custom chips, pushing management to project continuous heavy spending. Chief executive Sundar Pichai defended the strategy to financial analysts, describing the massive capital allocation as a long-range planning process rather than a short-term exercise.","Other technology behemoths faced similar investor skepticism regarding the financial sustainability of the ongoing artificial intelligence race. Amazon shares fell 6% in after-hours trading after the retailer reported quarterly sales growth of 11% to reach $201 billion, accompanied by a staggering negative cash flow figure of $42 billion. Chief executive Andy Jassy acknowledged the heavy spending, explaining that the enterprise is aggressively funding future opportunities in computer chips and its Bedrock AI developer platform. Jassy admitted that while spreading the costs over decades would be more convenient, market realities demand immediate, aggressive investment to secure long-term market positions.","Meanwhile, Microsoft experienced a milder reaction from Wall Street, with its share price slipping by less than 1%. The company reported revenue growth of 19% to reach $92.3 billion, alongside a 30% increase in its crucial cloud business. Chief executive Satya Nadella highlighted strong enterprise demand and surging adoption of the Copilot AI assistant, noting that automated tasks have nearly doubled. Nevertheless, industry experts note that the contrasting financial updates from these technology leaders underscore a profound uncertainty across the industry regarding where and when massive artificial intelligence investments will ultimately generate sustainable profits."],"facts":[{"fact":"Google parent Alphabet lost just over $500bn in value on Thursday after its update rattled Wall Street.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Alphabet's stock hit a six-month low after it revealed AI summaries on search were affecting ad revenue.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Alphabet net profit slid 25% from a year earlier to $26.2bn, while revenue rose 25% to $127.6bn.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Google Cloud revenue grew by 103% to nearly $31bn.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Alphabet reported a negative free cash flow in excess of $9bn for the quarter.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Amazon shares fell 6% after hours following results showing quarterly sales growth of 11% to $201bn and negative cash flow of $42bn.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Microsoft shares fell by less than 1% as its revenue grew 19% to $92.3bn and cloud business grew 30% to $63bn.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"technology","lemma":"technology","pos":"noun","he":"טכנולוגיה","name":false},{"text":"sector","lemma":"sector","pos":"noun","he":"סקטור, מגזר","name":false},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experience","pos":"verb","he":"חווה","name":false},{"text":"severe","lemma":"severe","pos":"adjective","he":"חמור","name":false},{"text":"market","lemma":"market","pos":"noun","he":"שוק","name":false},{"text":"reaction","lemma":"reaction","pos":"noun","he":"תגובה","name":false},{"text":"astronomical","lemma":"astronomical","pos":"adjective","he":"אסטרונומי","name":false},{"text":"financial","lemma":"financial","pos":"adjective","he":"פיננסי","name":false},{"text":"commitments","lemma":"commitment","pos":"noun","he":"התחייבויות","name":false},{"text":"artificial","lemma":"artificial"